        "790afa5fd340f67b53187d28beb1a64b9c3c0ea5"
      ],
      "title": "bthci_evt: Fix dissection of CS mode3 step",
      "message": "bthci_evt: Fix dissection of CS mode3 step\n\nWhen calling `dissect_bthci_evt_cs_mode2_step` to dissect a CS mode3\nstep the `step_data_length` must be the remaining data length after\ndissecting the mode1 part of the mode3 step using\n`dissect_bthci_evt_cs_mode1_step`.\n\nThis change fixes a bug where the number of tones added by\n`dissect_bthci_evt_cs_mode2_step` when dissecting mode3 steps was too\nhigh. This would cause not only invalid parsing of the current mode3\nstep but also the rest of the subevent result/ subevent continue result\nevent would be corrupted.\n",
      "author_name": "Erik Sandgren",
      "author_email": "erik.sandgren@nordicsemi.no",
      "authored_date": "2024-12-18T08:07:15.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "Alexis La Goutte",
      "committer_email": "alexis.lagoutte@gmail.com",
